  - discrete-time control
  - system identification
  - scientific computing
  - engineering education
abstract: >-
  A from-scratch, validated NumPy implementation of linear control theory: models and realisations, time and
  frequency response, stability tests, the root locus and the Nyquist criterion, PID and lead/lag design,
  pole placement, observers, LQR, Kalman filtering and LQG, discretisation and digital design, robustness and
  fundamental limitations, system identification, model reduction and MIMO basics, with ten example plants,
  course data and a 20-notebook course with worked solutions.
